/// - `ffi.invalid_handle` — `handle` is `0` (null) or the borrow yields `None`.
/// - `ffi.null_pointer` — `data` is a null pointer.
/// - `ffi.invalid_argument` — `data` does not verify as a `DuplicateRequest` buffer, or its `kind`
/// is not `Duplicate`.
/// - `jj.invalid_input` — `onto` with `insert_after`/`insert_before` (clap's refusal: before the
/// snapshot, nothing written, no `precondition`); "Cannot duplicate the root commit"; a location
/// that would create a loop or resolves no parent; a merge with the root commit as a parent in a
/// Git repo; detail in `context`.
/// - `jj.change_not_found` — an id is malformed, carried by no VISIBLE commit, or divergent; the id
/// in `context`.
/// - `jj.revset_resolution_error` — the default `@` in a workspace with no working-copy commit.
/// - `jj.immutable` — a child `insert_after`/`insert_before` would rewrite is immutable.
/// - `jj.config_error` — the duplicate-description template setting is not a string or does not
/// parse, or the config or its `immutable_heads()` alias does not read or resolve.
/// - `jj.stale_working_copy` — the pre-verb snapshot found the working copy stale (Story 9.26).
/// - `jj.jj_lib_error` — an underlying jj-lib failure; detail in `context`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `handle` must be a value returned by a successful `zanshin_repo_open`, `zanshin_repo_init`,
/// `zanshin_repo_clone`, or `zanshin_repo_convert` that has not been closed. `0` is detected and
/// returned as `ffi.invalid_handle`. A stale non-zero handle is undefined behaviour; the Dart
/// worker's Model-A handle table (Story 3.9) makes a stale handle unreachable.
/// `data` must be null or point to `len` bytes of a caller-owned buffer built and owned/freed by
/// Dart (`fbs.DuplicateRequestObjectBuilder(...).toBytes()`); Rust only borrows it for the
/// duration of the call.
/// The returned token must be freed exactly once via `zanshin_buffer_free_token`.
@ffi.Native<ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> Function(ffi.Uint64, ffi.Pointer<ffi.Uint8>, ffi.UintPtr)>()
external ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> zanshin_duplicate(
  int handle,
  ffi.Pointer<ffi.Uint8> data,
  int len,
);

/// Switch the working copy to `change_id` without creating a new commit, in the repo
/// referenced by `handle`.
///
/// Returns a `FlatBuffers` `Envelope` carrying a `MutationResult` payload on success. Editing
/// the commit that already is `@` writes no operation and `new_op_id` is the pre-call head (the
/// CLI's "Already editing that commit."); an immutable `@` still refuses.
///
/// # Errors
/// - `ffi.invalid_handle` — `handle` is `0` (null) or the borrow yields `None`.
/// - `ffi.null_pointer` — `change_id` is a null pointer.
/// - `ffi.utf8_error` — `change_id` is not valid UTF-8.
/// - `jj.change_not_found` — `change_id` is malformed, absent, only-hidden, or divergent.
/// - `jj.immutable` — `change_id` resolves to a commit inside the repo's effective
/// immutable set; the offending hex commit id in `context`. Unlike `zanshin_describe`
/// and `zanshin_abandon`, this wrapper has no separate root-commit guard, so editing the
/// ROOT commit reports this code too (which is what the jj CLI reports for it).
/// - `jj.config_error` — the repo's jj config, or its
/// `revset-aliases."immutable_heads()"`, could not be read/parsed/resolved, so the
/// immutable set is unknown; detail in `context`.
/// - `jj.stale_working_copy` — the pre-verb snapshot found the working copy stale (Story 9.26);
/// the cause and both operation ids in `context`, nothing is written.
/// - `jj.jj_lib_error` — an underlying jj-lib failure; detail in `context`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `handle` must be a value returned by a successful `zanshin_repo_open`,
/// `zanshin_repo_init`, `zanshin_repo_clone`, or `zanshin_repo_convert` that has not
/// been closed. `0` is detected and returned as `ffi.invalid_handle`. A stale
/// non-zero handle is undefined behaviour; the Dart worker's Model-A handle table
/// (Story 3.9) makes a stale handle unreachable.
/// `change_id` must be a NUL-terminated UTF-8 C string owned by the caller (Dart
/// allocates via `toNativeUtf8()` and frees with `calloc.free()` after this call
/// returns — AR-P-5 inbound rule). Rust only borrows it for the duration of the call.
/// The returned token must be freed exactly once via `zanshin_buffer_free_token`.
@ffi.Native<ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> Function(ffi.Uint64, ffi.Pointer<ffi.Char>)>()
external ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> zanshin_edit(
  int handle,
  ffi.Pointer<ffi.Char> change_id,
);

